/// Static, human-readable documentation of the LASA backend public API.
/// This mixin declares exactly one method and reads no actor state.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# LASA Backend API\n\nLASA ('A Journey Through Local and Global Flavors') is a food-and-culture site.\nThe backend stores visitor-submitted reviews, comments, and suggestions, plus\neach visitor's favorites and Flavor Passport stamps. All data is persisted in\nthe canister's stable state and survives upgrades.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- **No accounts and no login.** There is no registration step and no user\n  profile. Every caller — including an anonymous one — has a stable\n  'Principal' identity supplied by the Internet Computer.\n- **Anonymous callers still have a stable principal.** An anonymous caller's\n  principal is derived from the caller's connection, so it is stable for the\n  duration of that session but is not a durable identity across devices.\n- **Per-caller data is keyed by principal.** 'toggleFavorite', 'listFavorites',\n  'markExplored', and 'listExplored' read and write rows owned by the calling\n  principal. Two different principals never see each other's favorites or\n  passport stamps.\n- **Community content is public.** 'listReviews', 'getReviewStats',\n  'listComments', and 'listSuggestions' are open reads and return data\n  submitted by all visitors.\n- **Identity derivation.** The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity\n  derivation origin, published at '/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin' when\n  available. An agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity\n  authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for\n  example 'icp identity link web <name> --app <host>'). Such a delegation acts\n  with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- **No registration prerequisite.** Unlike role-gated apps, no endpoint here\n  requires a prior registration call; every public method is callable directly.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- **'foodId'** is a 'Nat' identifying one of the six featured foods (1..6 in the\n  LASA catalog). It is not validated against a catalog on the backend.\n- **'createdAt'** is a 'Nat' timestamp in **nanoseconds since the Unix epoch**\n  (UTC). Divide by 1,000,000,000 for seconds.\n- **'rating'** is a 'Nat' star count, valid range **1..5** inclusive.\n- **'average'** is a 'Float' star average, '0.0' when a food has no reviews.\n- **'name'** on a suggestion is '?Text' — 'null' when the visitor left it blank.\n- **'category'** is a variant: '#filipinoFood', '#internationalFood', '#topic',\n  or '#websiteImprovement'.\n- **'owner'** is a 'Principal' (the caller who created the row).\n\n## Public methods\n\n### Reviews\n\n- 'submitReview(input : ReviewInput) : async Review' — submit a review.\n  'ReviewInput' is '{ foodId : Nat; reviewerName : Text; rating : Nat;\n  text : Text }'. Returns the stored 'Review' with its assigned 'id' and\n  'createdAt'.\n- 'listReviews() : async [Review]' — all reviews, **newest first** (descending\n  'id').\n- 'getReviewStats(foodId : Nat) : async ReviewStats' — '{ foodId; count;\n  average }' for one food. 'average' is '0.0' when 'count' is '0'.\n\n### Comments\n\n- 'submitComment(input : CommentInput) : async Comment' — leave a comment.\n  'CommentInput' is '{ foodId : Nat; authorName : Text; text : Text }'.\n- 'listComments() : async [Comment]' — all comments, **newest first**.\n\n### Suggestions\n\n- 'submitSuggestion(input : SuggestionInput) : async Suggestion' — submit a\n  suggestion. 'SuggestionInput' is '{ name : ?Text; text : Text;\n  category : SuggestionCategory }'.\n- 'listSuggestions() : async [Suggestion]' — all suggestions, **newest first**.\n\n### Favorites (per caller)\n\n- 'toggleFavorite(foodId : Nat) : async Bool' — toggle a food as a favorite for\n  the caller. Returns 'true' when the food is now a favorite, 'false' when it\n  was removed.\n- 'listFavorites() : async [Nat]' — the caller's favorite food ids.\n\n### Flavor Passport (per caller)\n\n- 'markExplored(foodId : Nat) : async Bool' — mark a food as explored for the\n  caller. Stamps are permanent: re-marking an already-explored food returns\n  'true' and changes nothing.\n- 'listExplored() : async [Nat]' — the caller's explored food ids.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- 'getApiDoc() : async Text' — this document.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- All writes are synchronous update calls that complete in one message; there\n  is no job queue, no async processing, and no pending state to poll.\n- Reads ('listReviews', 'getReviewStats', 'listComments', 'listSuggestions',\n  'listFavorites', 'listExplored', 'getApiDoc') are 'query' calls: fast,\n  unreplicated, and read-only.\n- To refresh a list after a write, simply call the corresponding list method\n  again; there is no cursor or version token.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- 'submitReview', 'submitComment', and 'submitSuggestion' are **not\n  idempotent**: each successful call appends a new row with a fresh 'id'. A\n  retried call creates a duplicate. Do not blindly retry after a timeout.\n- 'toggleFavorite' is **not idempotent**: calling it twice returns the food to\n  its original state. To set a known state, read 'listFavorites' first.\n- 'markExplored' **is idempotent**: marking the same food repeatedly is safe and\n  leaves the stamp in place.\n- No method deletes or overwrites existing rows.\n\n## Errors, traps, and limits\n\n- 'submitReview' traps with ''Rating must be between 1 and 5'' when 'rating' is\n  outside 1..5.\n- 'submitReview' traps with ''Review text must not be empty'' when 'text' is\n  empty or only spaces.\n- 'submitComment' traps with ''Comment text must not be empty'' when 'text' is\n  empty or only spaces.\n- 'submitSuggestion' traps with ''Suggestion text must not be empty'' when\n  'text' is empty or only spaces.\n- A trap rejects the whole message: nothing is stored and the caller receives an\n  opaque reject. Validate inputs client-side to avoid it.\n- 'reviewerName' and 'authorName' are **not** validated and may be empty; the\n  frontend should supply a display name or a fallback such as 'Guest'.\n- There is no pagination: list methods return every stored row. Very large\n  collections will eventually hit the message size limit.\n\n## Non-obvious gotchas\n\n- **Newest-first ordering** is by descending 'id', not by 'createdAt'; the two\n  agree because ids increase monotonically.\n- **'average' is '0.0', not 'null'**, when a food has no reviews — check\n  'count' to distinguish 'no reviews' from 'rated zero'.\n- **Favorites and passport are per principal.** An anonymous caller's data is\n  tied to that session's principal and is not recoverable from another device.\n- **The Flavor Passport has no server-side catalog.** The backend stores only\n  the explored 'foodId's; the frontend knows the six featured foods and computes\n  the collected/not-yet-explored progress count.\n- **OQL query surface.** The canister also exposes 'schema()' and 'execute()'\n  from the Caffeine Object Query Layer for the Data Intelligence agent. These\n  are separate from the methods above and are not part of the app's UI API."
  };
};
